  "gaps": [
    "The general education block is printed as 45 quarter credits ('Choose 45 quarter credits'). The remainder figure of 33 credits is derived, not printed: 45 minus the two required math courses (MAT1050 and MAT2051, 6 each). This derivation assumes the required math courses count toward the 45. The capture places them under 'General Education Requirements', and the section totals (45+51+30+42+12=180) support that reading, but the capture does not state it explicitly.",
    "The capture also requires a minimum of 4 quarter credits from each general education category (Communication, Humanities, Natural Science and Mathematics, Social Science). The specific course choices are student-selected and are not itemized in this ledger.",
    "Total requires a minimum of 54 quarter credits from the 3000-level and above. The capture does not specify how this interacts with elective selection.",
    "Capstone courses (IT4997, IT4998) must be taken during the student's final two quarters. The capture does not state whether they must be completed at Capella.",
    "No residency or institutional-credit (minimum credits completed at Capella) requirement is stated in the capture.",
    "No transfer credit limits or policies are stated in the capture.",
    "An optional Honors Pathway (PHI-H2005, COM-H4005, SOC-H3005; at least 15 quarter credits) is applied toward general education for honors students only. It is not included as a standard requirement.",
    "A FlexPath option uses program points (e.g., 22.5 program points for general education) rather than quarter credits. The capture does not give the FlexPath program-point breakdown for this specialization's core, specialization, elective and capstone courses.",
    "Course prerequisites are referenced ('Refer to the course descriptions') but are not included in the capture."
  ],
